1 REM ============================================================
2 REM  t69_security_deep.bpp
3 REM  BASIC++ Security System Test & Tutorial
4 REM ============================================================
5 REM
6 REM  BASIC++ implements a capability-based security system
7 REM  that controls which operations programs can perform.
8 REM
9 REM  SECURITY LEVELS:
10 REM    SEC_OPEN       - All operations allowed (default)
11 REM    SEC_TRUSTED    - File I/O and SHELL allowed
12 REM    SEC_SANDBOX    - No file, shell, or network access
13 REM    SEC_RESTRICTED - No PEEK/POKE, no I/O, no CHAIN
14 REM
15 REM  CAPABILITY FLAGS:
16 REM    CAP_IO         - File and device I/O
17 REM    CAP_NET        - Network access
18 REM    CAP_USB        - USB device access
19 REM    CAP_SHELL      - Shell/system command execution
20 REM    CAP_MEMORY     - PEEK/POKE access
21 REM    CAP_COMPILE    - COMPILE command access
22 REM
23 REM  SECURITY COMMANDS:
24 REM    SECURITY SHOW   - Display current security level
25 REM    SECURITY LEVEL  - Show active capabilities
26 REM
27 REM  When a blocked operation is attempted, an error is
28 REM  raised and execution stops (or goes to error handler).
29 REM
30 DIALECT "GWBS"
31 REM
100 REM === SECURITY SHOW ===
101 REM Displays the current security level and capabilities.
110 TEST "SECURITY SHOW"
120 SECURITY SHOW
130 REM Should print: Security Level: OPEN
140 REM and list all active capabilities
150 ENDTEST
200 REM === Default level is SEC_OPEN ===
201 REM In SEC_OPEN, all operations are allowed.
202 REM This is the default for interactive use.
210 TEST "Default security level"
220 REM We can do file I/O
230 OPEN "sec_test.tmp" FOR OUTPUT AS #1
240 PRINT #1, "test"
250 CLOSE #1
260 KILL "sec_test.tmp"
270 REM We can PEEK/POKE
280 POKE 3000, 42
290 ASSERT PEEK(3000)=42
300 ENDTEST
9999 END
